{"id":"word:hebrew:H1320","type":"word","title":"בָּשָׂר","subtitle":"H1320 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"flesh (from its freshness ); by extension, body , person ; also (by euphemistically) the pudenda of a man","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to בָּשָׂר (H1320) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 270 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"בָּשָׂר (bâsâr) means flesh (from its freshness ); by extension, body , person ; also (by euphemistically) the pudenda of a man First listed occurrence: 1Chr 11 1."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"בָּשָׂר","transliteration":"bâsâr","pronunciation":"baw-sawr'","strong":"H1320","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1320","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["בָּשָׂ֑ר","בָּשָׂ֖ר","בְּשָׂר֖/וֹ","בְּשַׂ֣ר","בָּשָֽׂר"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",88],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",39],["HNcmsc",29],["HTd/Ncmsa",25],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",11],["HC/Ncmsa",8],["HR/Ncmsc",8],["HNcmsc/Sp3mp",7],["HNcmsc/Sp2ms",6],["HC/Ncmsc/Sp1cs",5]]},"definitions":{"short":"flesh (from its freshness ); by extension, body , person ; also (by euphemistically) the pudenda of a man","usage":"body, (fat, lean) flesh(-ed), kin, (man-) kind, nakedness, self, skin.","full":"H1320. basar בָּשָׂר 266 noun masculine flesh (compare Arabic skin , Syriac , Assyrian bišru , blood-relation , Dl Assyrian Stud. i. 143, compare Pr. 170 , Sabean תורם בשר flesh of bulls ) — Gen 2:21 126t.; construct בְּשַׂר 17:11 40t.; suffix בּשָׂרִי etc. Psa 16:9 96t.; plural בְּשָׂרִים Prov 14:30 ; &#8212; 1 of the body: a. of animals Gen 41:2-19 Exod 21:28 ; 22:30 ; Num 12:12 (E) 11:4-33 (JE) Gen 9:4 + (P 30 t.) Deut 12:15 + (D 9 t.) Judg 6:19-21 1Sam 2:13 , 15 ; 1Kin 17:6 ; 19:21 ; Job 31:31 ; 41:15 ; Psa 50:13 ; Prov 23:20 ; Isa 22:13 ; 44:16 , 19 ; 65:4 ; 66:17 ; Jer 7:21 ; 11:15 ; Ezek 4:14 6 t. Dan 10:3 ; Hosea 8:13 ; Micah 3:3 ; Hag 2:12 ; Zech 11:9 , 16 . b. of men Gen 40:19 (E) 2:21 ; Exod 4:7 (J) Lev 12:3 ; 13:2 16 t. 26:29 (P) Deut 28:53 , 55 ; 32:42 ; Judg 8:7 ; 1Sam 17:44 ; 1Kin 4:34 ; 5:10 ; 5:14 ; 6:30 ; 1 Kings 9:36; Job 2:5 ; 4:15 ; 6:12 ; 7:5 ; 10:11 ; 13:14 ; 19:20 , 22 ; 21:6 ; 33:21 , 25 ; Psa 27:2 ; 38:4 ; 38:8 ; 79:2 ; 102:6 ; 109:24 ; Prov 4:22 ; 5:11 ; Isa 9:19 ; 17:4 ; 49:26 ; Jer 19:9 ; Lam 3:4 ; Ezek 32:5 ; 37:6 , 8 ; 39:17-18 , Dan 1:15 ; Zech 14:12 . The flesh of the body is contrasted with stone Ezek 11:19 ; 36:26 . 2 flesh for the body itself (especially in P): ייסך לא אדם בשׂר על upon the body of man it shall not be poured Exod 30:32 (P); בשׂרו על ילבשׁ בד מכנסי linen drawers shall he put on his body Lev 6:3 ; 16:4 (P); בשׂרו על שׂק וישׂם 1 Kings 2;:27; בשׂרו את ורחץ and he shall bath his body 14:9 ; 15:13 , 16 ; 16:24 , 26 , 28 ; 17:16 ; 22:6 ; Num 19:7-8 , (P); בכשׂרכם תתנו לא לנפשׁ שׂרט ye shall not put any cutting for any one in your body Lev 19:28 compare 21:5 (P); בשׂרם כל על תער והעבירו and they shall pass a razor over all their body Num 8:7 (P). Ecclesiastes uses בשׂר only in this sense Eccl 2:3 ; 4:5 ; 5:5 ; 11:10 ; 12:12 ; elsewhere this usage only in poetry; the body antithetical to נפשׁ Job 14:22 ; Isa 10:18 ; Psa 63:2 ; לב 16:9 ; 84:3 ; Prov 14:30 (only here emphatic plural = entire body Bö § 695 , Leiblichkeit De); מִבְּשָׂרִי apart from my body , in disembodied state Job 19:26 ; בשׂרי מפחדך סמר my body trembleth for fear of thee Psa 119:120 . 3 make organ of Generation (euphemism): עָרְלַתְכֶם בְּשַׂר Gen 17:11 , 14 , 23 , 24 , 25 (P); ערוה בשׂר Exod 28:42 (P), but בשׂר Gen 17:14 ; Lev 15:2-19 (P) Ezek 16:26 ; 23:20 ; 44:7 , 9 . 4 flesh for kindred, blood-relations: מבשׂרי ובשׂר מעצמי עצם bone of my bone and flesh of my flesh Gen 2:23 (J); אחד לבשׂר והיו and they shall become one flesh 2:24 (J); ובשׂרי עצמי 29:14 (J) Judg 9:2 ; 2Sam 5:1 ; 19:13 ; 19:14 ; 1Chr 11:1 ; בשׂר with suffix in same sense Gen 37:27 (J) Neh 5:5 ; Isa 58:7 , for which בשׂרו שְׁאֵר near of kin , man or woman Lev 18:6 ; 25:49 (both H; 25:49 || מִשְׁמָּחָה , compare RS k 149 ). 5 man over against God as frail or erring Gen 6:3 (J) Psa 56:5 ; 78:39 ; eyes of flesh Job 10:4 ; arm of flesh 2Chr 32:8 ; Jer 17:5 ; horses are flesh not spirit Isa 31:3 6 the phrase ׃כָּלבָּֿשָׂר a. all living beings Gen 6:17 , 19 ; 7:21 ; 9:11 , 15 , 16 , 17 ; Lev 17:14 ; Num 18:15 (P) Job 34:15 ; Psa 136:25 . b. animals Gen 7:15-16 , 8:17 (P). c. mankind Gen 6:12 , 18 ; Num 16:22 ; 27:16 (P) Deut 5:28 ; Psa 65:3 ; 145:21 ; Isa 40:5-6 , 49:26 ; 66:16 , 23 , 24 ; Jer 12:12 ; 25:31 ; 32:27 ; 45:5 ; Ezek 21:4 ; 21:9 ; 21:10 ; Joel 3:1 ; Zechariah 2:17; compare אישׁ בשׂר כל Job 12:10 .","rootNote":"from 1319 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 11 1","keyReferences":["1Chr 11 1","1Kgs 17 6","1Kgs 17 6","1Kgs 19 21","1Kgs 21 27","1Sam 2 13","1Sam 2 15","1Sam 2 15"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":270,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 11 1","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּֽ/בְשָׂרְ/ךָ֖","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsc/Sp2ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 17 6","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/בָשָׂר֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 17 6","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/בָשָׂ֖ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 19 21","book":"1Kgs","chapter":19,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/בָּשָׂ֔ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 21 27","book":"1Kgs","chapter":21,"verse":27,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּשָׂר֖/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 2 13","book":"1Sam","chapter":2,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/בָּשָׂ֔ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 2 15","book":"1Sam","chapter":2,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בָשָׂ֔ר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 2 